Here's how you can do it:

1. Create a new Shape Layer.
2. Add a Rectangle tool to draw a rectangle on the canvas (this will be used as a reference for the size).
3. Select the Rectangle tool and press "P" to reveal its properties panel.
4. In the Path section, click on the stopwatch icon next to "Path Expression" to enable expressions.
5. Replace the existing expression with the following code:

```javascript
// Define variables
var width = 500;
var height = 500;
var radius = 20; // Adjust this value to change the roundness

// Calculate control points
var p1 = [0, 0];
var p2 = [width - radius, 0];
var p3 = [width, radius];
var p4 = [width, height - radius];
var p5 = [width - radius, height];
var p6 = [radius, height];
var p7 = [0, height - radius];
var p8 = [0, radius];

